{
  "_comment": "Typed IaC intent v1 allow-list (docs/planning/typed-iac-intent-plan.md §2.4, amended by its Fable RT F5-F8). DATA, not code: shared/iac_intent.py interprets every key. A type is allowed only when it is listed under `types` AND the owner question it is gated on is answered `yes` in `owner_answers`; a different owner answer is a one-line data edit. Additions by PR + test only (Q-TI-3). Owner answers are PROVISIONAL (recorded 2026-10-18 while the owner was away; the plan RT agreed with every recommendation).",
  "schema": "iac_intent_allowed_types/v1",
  "owner_answers": {
    "Q-TI-3": {"answer": "yes", "status": "provisional", "text": "Approve the 17-type allow-list (16 google types + kubernetes_manifest), additions by PR + test only."},
    "Q-TI-4": {"answer": "yes", "status": "provisional", "text": "Allow random_id / random_password (random 3.7.1 is in the production mirror)."},
    "Q-TI-5": {"answer": "yes", "status": "provisional", "text": "Allow typed kubernetes_manifest in v1. Caveat (RT F8): `manifest` is cty `dynamic` in kubernetes 2.36.0, so only exact-path rules apply below it (no schema walk)."},
    "Q-TI-7": {"answer": "yes", "status": "provisional", "text": "An unknown type fails closed with IAC.TYPE_NOT_ALLOWED (the type is counted for a PR); no permissive mode."},
    "Q-TI-9": {"answer": "yes", "status": "provisional", "text": "Composite bundles stay out of intent v1 (they embed compute the topology owns)."}
  },
