  "_comment_target_ref_only": "RT TI-2 F1/F2 (TI-2b): IAM targets, data destinations, token identities and encryption keys take ONLY a reference of one of the listed shapes: [resource_attr, <type>, <attr>] of a resource this intent declares, [module_output, <catalog module>, <output>] of a module instance this intent declares, [fact, <fact>], or an `existing` user-owned address of a listed resource type. A literal is IAC.TARGET_REF_REQUIRED; a refused_blocks block is IAC.BLOCK_NOT_ALLOWED.",
  "_comment_refused_attributes": "RT TI-2b R2 (TI-2c): exact attribute paths that are never expressible (IAC.ATTRIBUTE_NOT_ALLOWED): the write-only twins of secret attributes, which would otherwise take a literal secret. A generated secret is written to secret_data / password (random_password_only). Any attribute the slice marks write_only is refused too."
